%% DM26-0670

%% A client subscribes to a topic, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md "The flows" and "Policy in the
%% broker"). The agent's own gate decides first by the same rule, so a refusal at the broker is a surprise, and is said to be.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Gate as the agent's gate and its authority
    participant Client as Agent (facade and transport)
    participant Listener
    participant Session as SessionAgent
    participant Broker
    participant Topics as TopicManager / TopicAgent
    participant Subs as SubscriberManager / SubscriberAgent

    Client->>Gate: subscribe, topic
    alt refused: its Cedar forbids it, or the computed set has no such topic and no permit
        Gate-->>Client: refused
        Client->>Client: kept as wanted, ClientEvent::SubscribeRefused, nothing sent<br/>(asked again when the agent's authority changes)
    else allowed
        Client->>Listener: SubscribeRequest(registration_id, topic)
        alt not registered, or another session's id
            Listener-->>Client: SubscribeAcknowledgment(Err "Bad request: ...")
        else Listener::decide: Cedar first, then the floor (p:sub), default deny
            Listener-->>Client: SubscribeAcknowledgment(Err reason)
            Client->>Client: ClientEvent::SubscribeRefused,<br/>and the agent's health says the broker refused what its gate let through
        else allowed
            Listener->>Session: SubscribeRequest(topic)
            Session->>Broker: SubscribeRequest(registration_id, topic)
            Broker->>Topics: ensure_topic_and_subscribe (a topic is created on first use)
            Topics->>Subs: CreateSubscriber(registration_id:topic)
            opt the session took over from a superseded one
                Subs->>Subs: inherit what its identity and instance held on this topic, oldest first (ClaimHeld)
            end
            Subs-->>Topics: SubscriberAgent
            Topics->>Topics: TopicAgent AddSubscriber, then TopicAttached to it,<br/>and what was queued for a first subscriber goes to it
            Topics-->>Client: SubscribeAcknowledgment(Ok), through the session's Listener
            Client->>Client: ClientEvent::ClientSubscribed
        end
    end

    Note over Listener,Client: Later, on every change of authority (JudgeSubscriptions), each Listener judges what its connection holds again.
    opt no longer allowed
        Listener->>Session: UnsubscribeRequest(topic)
        Listener-->>Client: SubscribeAcknowledgment(Err reason), unasked
    end
    opt the certificate is now revoked
        Listener->>Listener: the connection closes, the session kept for the retention window
    end
